{"id": 38, "ts": 1783017304.8279207, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I acknowledge the panel\u2019s consensus that Candidate\u202fC remains the strongest overall, especially given the solid evidence of 100\u202f% operational reliability, rapid correct decision\u2011making, calmness in crisis, and a crew\u2011focused attitude.\u202fHowever, we still lack critical data on responsibility and role maturity for Candidates\u202fA and\u202fB, which are essential for long\u2011distance flights.\u202fFrom the latest input, only Candidate\u202fD has a clear responsibility indicator (\u201ctakes responsibility seriously\u201d), while A and B have no such evidence.\u202fThis reinforces my view that, despite the missing feedback\u2011orientation evidence for C, the alternatives either lack reliability (A,\u202fB,\u202fD) or exhibit serious crew\u2011cooperation issues (B,\u202fD) and, in the case of A, also lack any demonstrated responsibility.\u202fTherefore, I maintain my provisional recommendation for Candidate\u202fC, but I recommend we keep the responsibility gap for A and B in mind should any new evidence emerge."}
